# Scratch projects the suite builds under test/. They are removed on teardown,
# but a crashed or interrupted run leaves them behind, and only the
# .test-data-server-* pattern above was ignored — so an interrupted run followed
# by `git add -A` could commit fixture junk. Cover the whole family instead of
# naming each one, since new suites keep adding them:
# .test-explain-project, .test-keyword-project, .test-routing-project, ...
test/.test-*/

